# Dev-server-only relaxation, mirroring `app.security.devCsp` in
# src-tauri/tauri.conf.json. It is never part of a production build.
#
# Why each exception is needed:
#   script-src 'unsafe-inline'  @vitejs/plugin-react injects the React Refresh
#                               preamble as an inline module script.
#   script-src 'unsafe-eval'    Vite's dev module runner / react-refresh.
#   style-src  'unsafe-inline'  Vite injects CSS as inline <style> tags in dev.
#   connect-src ws://…:1420     HMR websocket, loopback only.
#
# LAN dev mode (PORTPAL_ALLOW_LAN=1) serves HMR from a LAN address, which this
# loopback-only connect-src blocks on purpose. Override locally in
# `.env.development.local` if you deliberately opt into LAN exposure.
# `frame-ancestors` is intentionally absent here: browsers ignore it when the
# policy arrives via <meta>. It lives in `app.security.csp` in tauri.conf.json,
# which Tauri serves as a real Content-Security-Policy header where it applies.
#
# style-src/font-src carry the two Google Fonts origins ONLY because
# src/styles/tokens.css still @imports the Geist / JetBrains Mono webfonts.
# See docs/dependency-audit.md -> "Known gap: remote webfonts". Vendor the
# woff2 files locally and these two origins come straight back out.
VITE_CSP=default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' 'unsafe-eval'; style-src 'self' https://fonts.googleapis.com 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com data:; connect-src 'self' ipc: http://ipc.localhost ws://localhost:1420 ws://127.0.0.1:1420 http://localhost:1420 http://127.0.0.1:1420; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; frame-src 'none'; form-action 'none'
